{% set local_problem %}
<p>Cullman's tree-lined streets and mature landscaping are part of what makes this community attractive. But all those trees — oaks, pines, maples, and more — produce debris ending up in your gutters. Pine needles accumulate year-round. Hardwood leaves blanket everything in fall. Seeds, twigs, and pollen add to spring accumulation.</p>

<p>Without protection, Cullman gutters typically need cleaning 2-4 times yearly. That's either time you spend on ladders (dangerous for two-story homes) or $150-200+ per professional cleaning. Over years, those costs compound significantly.</p>

<p>More importantly, clogged gutters cause damage. Water overflows against your foundation, soaks into fascia boards, and erodes landscaping. For homeowners who maintain their properties carefully — and Cullman has many — gutter clogs undermine that effort.</p>

<p><strong>Our strong opinion:</strong> Don't buy foam gutter inserts from the hardware store. We've pulled thousands of feet of failed foam out of Cullman County gutters. They decompose in Alabama humidity, trap debris inside instead of keeping it out, and become part of the clog within 18-24 months. Spend on micro-mesh or don't bother at all.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Gutter guards are covers or screens fitting over or inside your gutters. They allow water to enter while blocking leaves, pine needles, and debris. The debris either blows away or sits on top where it eventually dries and falls off.</p>

<p><strong>What works in Cullman:</strong> Micro-mesh guards with surgical-grade stainless steel screen. Holes around 50 microns — small enough to block even fine pine needles and pollen. Water sheets through; debris stays on top.</p>

<p><strong>What doesn't work here:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Foam inserts — decompose in humidity within 2 years</li>
<li>Plastic snap-in screens — warp in Alabama heat, don't block fine debris</li>
<li>Brush-style guards — pine needles embed in bristles, nearly impossible to clean</li>
</ul>

<p>For <a href="/recent-projects/">Cullman's historic homes</a> with half-round gutters, we offer guard options designed specifically for that profile — protection without compromising period-appropriate appearance.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've installed guards throughout Cullman County for over 20 years. We know which types work best for the area's mix of pine and hardwood trees, and we take care to recommend solutions matching both your debris challenges and your home's character.</p>

<p>Quality guards, properly installed, provide years of reliable protection. That's what we deliver.</p>

<p><strong>Warning:</strong> Be skeptical of gutter guard companies offering "lifetime" cleaning guarantees. Read the fine print. Most exclude "maintenance debris" — defined broadly enough to cover almost everything. We're upfront: guards reduce cleaning 90%+, not 100%. Occasional surface maintenance happens.</p>
{% endset %}
